WEBVTT

00:04.546 --> 00:06.380
THE FOLLOWING CONTENT CONTAINS DEPICTIONS
OF DOMESTIC ABUSE.

00:06.381 --> 00:07.548
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

00:12.012 --> 00:13.222
Aren't you tired? Huh?

00:14.014 --> 00:15.348
Why don't you come sit down?

00:15.349 --> 00:17.016
Let's talk a little
and figure this out.

00:20.771 --> 00:24.106
If you give me the gold bar
and the knife, we can talk.

00:24.107 --> 00:25.651
Ugh, you're being really annoying.

00:33.492 --> 00:35.244
Closer.

00:39.790 --> 00:40.791
And the knife.

00:58.141 --> 01:01.602
You need to think about this
from an economic perspective, okay?

01:01.603 --> 01:04.480
It really doesn't matter
if it's gold or drugs.

01:04.481 --> 01:07.275
All that matters
is raking in the dough.

01:07.276 --> 01:09.277
Can we turn that item into money or not?

01:09.278 --> 01:12.613
You really think taking the gold bar
to a jewelry shop's a good idea?

01:12.614 --> 01:15.074
A 10-kilogram bar
with a foreign stamp on it?

01:16.535 --> 01:18.536
Okay, just listen.

01:18.537 --> 01:22.123
The jewelry shops, the pawn shops even,
they're all linked to who I work for.

01:22.124 --> 01:25.001
Stuff like gold bars,
that's gonna get around.

01:25.002 --> 01:27.295
You wanna sell a gold bar,
you gotta hand over your phone number,

01:27.296 --> 01:29.213
name, and ID.
So what?

01:29.214 --> 01:31.424
You'll write down,
"Kim Heeju, ID 123?"

01:31.425 --> 01:34.594
You think you can handle all this alone?
You can't.

01:34.595 --> 01:36.512
But I can.
I'm telling you.

01:36.513 --> 01:37.848
My methods are solid.

01:41.059 --> 01:42.518
How do we do it, then?

01:42.519 --> 01:44.812
You a bit more interested now?

01:44.813 --> 01:48.316
Okay, before I lay all this out,
let's make a deal.

01:48.317 --> 01:50.359
- Hey, get back!
-  Like partners.

01:50.360 --> 01:52.111
I said get back. Go.

01:52.112 --> 01:53.446
Talk from there.

02:02.164 --> 02:04.874
Okay, first, where's the casket?

02:04.875 --> 02:06.668
This can't be everything.

02:07.919 --> 02:09.086
Just tell me where it is.

02:09.087 --> 02:10.921
I need to know exactly
how many bars there are

02:10.922 --> 02:12.089
before I can put a plan together.

02:12.090 --> 02:14.051
Why should I even trust you?

02:15.344 --> 02:16.845
I literally just told you!

02:17.679 --> 02:19.972
If I was gonna rat you out to the boss,
I would have done it already,

02:19.973 --> 02:21.141
and all the guys would be here.

02:23.644 --> 02:26.480
Fine, I wasn't gonna tell you this.
Guess I have to, though.

02:28.148 --> 02:29.440
Look.

02:29.441 --> 02:32.110
That shit hurt.
It still hurts.

02:32.903 --> 02:35.696
They were gonna cut off my ear
if I didn't start talking.

02:35.697 --> 02:37.156
But I held out.

02:37.157 --> 02:40.242
You know why?
'Cause I thought of you.

02:40.243 --> 02:41.911
What the hell?

02:41.912 --> 02:43.704
Why am I such a softie?

02:43.705 --> 02:45.331
Don't make me laugh.

02:45.332 --> 02:48.334
The only reason you showed up here
was to look for the drugs.

02:48.335 --> 02:50.252
If you couldn't find them
you would have threatened me

02:50.253 --> 02:52.296
or done whatever it took
to make me talk.

02:52.297 --> 02:54.298
And once you found them,
you would have killed me.

02:54.299 --> 02:56.425
Oh, really?
Correct me if I'm wrong here,

02:56.426 --> 02:58.762
but you were the one threatening
to shoot me.

03:00.597 --> 03:03.058
Okay, I get it.
Let's move on.

03:03.975 --> 03:05.142
How about this?

03:05.143 --> 03:07.061
Don't tell me where to find the gold.

03:07.062 --> 03:08.480
I won't ask, either.

03:09.147 --> 03:10.231
If you think I'd kill you

03:10.232 --> 03:13.401
and make a run for it after finding out
where the gold is, don't tell me.

03:13.402 --> 03:15.444
If I have no idea,
there's no problem, right?

03:15.445 --> 03:16.988
Instead, how's this?

03:18.115 --> 03:20.408
Every three days,
you give me one gold bar.

03:20.409 --> 03:23.744
Then it'll be up to me
to sell it and bring you the cash.

03:23.745 --> 03:25.663
That means I won't be able
to pull anything funny

03:25.664 --> 03:26.831
until we've sold all the gold.

03:26.832 --> 03:27.916
Make sense?

03:29.918 --> 03:31.001
How many are there?

03:31.002 --> 03:32.586
That I need to know.

03:37.759 --> 03:38.760
There's ten.

03:44.599 --> 03:45.766
Ten?

03:45.767 --> 03:50.187
If we sell one for a billion,
times ten is ten billion.

03:50.188 --> 03:51.355
Split it in half.

03:51.356 --> 03:52.606
-  Five billion each.
- Split it?

03:54.734 --> 03:56.777
You think it's just you and me?
:cue

03:56.778 --> 03:59.864
It's not our gold.
It belongs to Dokyung.

03:59.865 --> 04:01.073
What? Lee Dokyung?

04:01.074 --> 04:02.700
Nah, he's gonna die soon.

04:02.701 --> 04:05.286
And even if he lives,
he's going to jail anyway.

04:05.287 --> 04:07.163
Wait, why not just cut him out?

04:07.164 --> 04:08.540
What'd you say?

04:09.458 --> 04:10.792
Oh.

04:12.002 --> 04:13.003
What, are you dating?

04:13.920 --> 04:16.213
Am I right?
Is he your boyfriend?

04:16.214 --> 04:18.382
Eh, doesn't matter.

04:18.383 --> 04:20.134
How is it Lee Dokyung's?

04:20.135 --> 04:21.635
You realize he stole it, right?

04:21.636 --> 04:23.221
So it really belongs to Chairman An.

04:23.972 --> 04:25.056
Okay, then.

04:26.850 --> 04:29.059
So the three of us will split it.

04:29.060 --> 04:30.936
You'll get exactly one-third of the money.

04:30.937 --> 04:32.105
That's your share.

04:33.315 --> 04:34.316
Okay.

04:34.858 --> 04:35.859
Okay!

04:38.403 --> 04:40.613
- So, then.
-  What?

04:40.614 --> 04:42.948
-  We should fist bump so that...
- Don't come any closer!

04:42.949 --> 04:45.243
Well, we gotta lock in our contract, so...

04:46.620 --> 04:47.746
...fist bump to seal the deal.

04:49.247 --> 04:51.792
First you have to tell me how you plan
on selling the gold bars.

04:52.250 --> 04:53.793
Explain that.
Then I'll decide.

04:53.794 --> 04:55.253
Are you serious?

04:56.296 --> 04:57.297
What the...

04:58.423 --> 05:00.591
Fine. Listen carefully.

05:00.592 --> 05:05.012
Gold is traded in hundreds
of forms in shops across the country.

05:05.013 --> 05:07.765
Gold rings, gold pigs, random stuff.

05:07.766 --> 05:09.850
And the gold bar.

05:09.851 --> 05:14.438
The one-kilogram bars are the easiest ones
for us to trade.

05:14.439 --> 05:18.400
Everything changes depending on
the weight, purity,

05:18.401 --> 05:19.860
and where it was manufactured.

05:19.861 --> 05:23.864
So first we gotta break these down
into one-kilo bars

05:23.865 --> 05:25.450
- and recast them.
-  Who can do that?

05:26.368 --> 05:28.452
-  You?
-  No.

05:28.453 --> 05:30.704
We'll obviously need a goldsmith for that.

05:30.705 --> 05:32.706
Then there's the actual sale.

05:32.707 --> 05:35.251
Selling a 10-kilo bar would be hard,

05:35.252 --> 05:36.919
but small ones, well,

05:36.920 --> 05:39.005
jewelry stores have
no problem buying those.

05:39.923 --> 05:43.217
All of Gwangwon-do has ties to our company
so that won't work.

05:43.218 --> 05:45.386
I'll have to go to jewelry stores
in other areas

05:45.387 --> 05:47.721
and sell only one bar per store.

05:47.722 --> 05:50.099
The whole process of recasting
a bar to selling it

05:50.100 --> 05:53.394
shouldn't take any more than, say,
three days.

05:53.395 --> 05:56.021
So selling them all should take a month.

05:56.022 --> 05:57.898
And to avoid being tracked by the cops,

05:57.899 --> 06:00.359
we gotta make all
of our transactions in cash.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.612
Not to mention, we'll need fake IDs,
burner phones, and burner bank accounts.

06:03.613 --> 06:07.116
But I'll be taking care of all that,
so don't you worry about a thing.

06:07.117 --> 06:08.785
SAMJIN GOLD EXCHANGE

06:11.830 --> 06:15.125
And Heeju,
let's make one thing clear.

06:16.918 --> 06:19.295
Until we've sold all ten gold bars
and split the cash,

06:19.296 --> 06:20.714
we trust each other.

06:22.757 --> 06:26.052
Never, seriously never...

06:27.012 --> 06:30.472
Ever, ever, ever,
never betray each other.

06:30.473 --> 06:32.893
Do you promise?
If not, we're both dead.

06:33.852 --> 06:36.812
You'll be discovered in that mining town
hanging from your neck.

06:36.813 --> 06:38.689
And as for me,
I'm screwing the company over, too,

06:38.690 --> 06:42.319
so I'll get something chopped off
and become a cripple.

06:45.030 --> 06:46.323
You know what I'm saying?

06:50.577 --> 06:52.411
You're the one I'm worried about.

06:58.209 --> 06:59.711
Okay.

07:03.548 --> 07:05.049
Do this to sign the contract.

07:05.050 --> 07:07.218
Hmm? Deal?

07:13.266 --> 07:15.684
You gotta say "deal" when you do it.
That's how it works.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.102
Deal.

07:21.858 --> 07:22.859
Deal.

07:29.115 --> 07:30.116
Finally.

07:32.827 --> 07:35.830
:cue

08:16.538 --> 08:21.333
EPISODE 3
PARTNERSHIP

08:21.334 --> 08:22.335
Yeah.

08:27.424 --> 08:29.967
Goodness.

08:39.811 --> 08:41.979
Careful.
Ugh, shit.

08:44.566 --> 08:46.150
SEOYOON, YERIN, I'M SORRY FOR GOING FIRST.
TO EVERYONE WHO WAS HARMED BECAUSE OF ME,

08:46.151 --> 08:47.610
I AM SORRY. THIS IS THE LAST CHOICE
I CAN MAKE. I'M SORRY. I'M SO SORRY.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.238
Hold up. Stop.

09:04.961 --> 09:06.087
Go, yeah.

09:08.173 --> 09:09.339
Should I send him to forensics?

09:09.340 --> 09:10.799
Nah, just the morgue is fine.

09:10.800 --> 09:11.967
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

09:11.968 --> 09:13.385
The morgue.

09:19.559 --> 09:21.393
- Take him to the morgue.
-  Understood.

09:28.693 --> 09:30.861
Ah, I did it. Yeah.

09:30.862 --> 09:33.072
I took care of it like you asked.

09:33.073 --> 09:34.783
Who wrote that note, though?

09:35.992 --> 09:37.786
Looked like President Go's handwriting.

09:39.788 --> 09:41.914
You gotta stop with all
these useless theatrics.

09:41.915 --> 09:44.334
It's a waste.
Just keep your guys in line.

09:45.460 --> 09:46.544
Thanks for your work.

09:47.712 --> 09:49.379
See you soon, Detective.

09:49.380 --> 09:50.423
Sounds good.

09:52.383 --> 09:55.260
GANGWON SAEBAEK HOSPITAL

10:07.565 --> 10:09.359
What the hell have we been doing all day?

10:10.026 --> 10:12.027
We left the shop unattended.

10:12.028 --> 10:13.403
Ms. Yeo Sunok.

10:13.404 --> 10:15.240
Here. Come on.

10:24.499 --> 10:25.874
Hello.

10:25.875 --> 10:27.417
Could the patient wait outside?

10:27.418 --> 10:29.253
I'd like to speak with the guardian first.

10:29.254 --> 10:32.089
- Uh...
- You can just talk.

10:32.090 --> 10:33.591
I already know anyway.

10:37.345 --> 10:41.640
You were diagnosed here a year ago,
but you never went to another hospital?

10:41.641 --> 10:43.433
No.

10:43.434 --> 10:45.352
We should
have started treatment then.

10:45.353 --> 10:46.813
We're a little late now.

10:47.814 --> 10:49.022
If you look here,

10:49.023 --> 10:52.317
you'll see that the tumor cells
have metastasized to the lungs.

10:53.611 --> 10:56.614
Were you feeling okay?
I imagine the pain would be quite severe.

10:57.866 --> 11:00.159
Could surgery be an option?

11:00.160 --> 11:01.911
She should get hospitalized first.

11:02.662 --> 11:04.204
I recommend an examination,

11:04.205 --> 11:06.748
then beginning chemotherapy
to slow down the metastasis.

11:06.749 --> 11:08.917
As for surgery,

11:08.918 --> 11:11.212
let's see how things progress
and then decide.

11:11.796 --> 11:14.548
- 'Kay.
- So my cancer's in the final stage.

11:14.549 --> 11:16.341
Wouldn't surgery be useless?

11:16.342 --> 11:19.136
Well, when it comes to stages,

11:19.137 --> 11:20.304
you could say that, however...

11:20.305 --> 11:21.513
How much longer do I have?

11:21.514 --> 11:24.725
A specific time frame
is hard to determine at this point.

11:24.726 --> 11:26.686
If I get treatment, I can live...

11:27.270 --> 11:28.687
...how much longer?
Into my 80s?

11:28.688 --> 11:31.648
- Auntie.
-  I knew it'd be like this.

11:31.649 --> 11:33.151
They wanna fill me with drugs...

11:33.818 --> 11:36.278
...and poke me with needles even though
I'm dying anyway.

11:36.279 --> 11:39.656
That's how hospitals make money, isn't it?
Hey, we're leaving.

11:39.657 --> 11:40.991
- Auntie!
- Get up. I'm done with all this.

11:40.992 --> 11:42.869
Auntie, please wait! Seriously!

11:44.120 --> 11:45.121
:cue

11:46.664 --> 11:48.874
- Auntie.
- Just forget it.

11:48.875 --> 11:51.210
Oh, come on, please!

11:51.211 --> 11:52.711
I said forget it!

11:52.712 --> 11:54.546
These guys are all crooks.

11:54.547 --> 11:56.465
They don't deserve our hard-earned money.

11:56.466 --> 11:59.092
If this is really about the money,
don't worry.

11:59.093 --> 12:00.886
- I have it.
-  Where? Show me.

12:00.887 --> 12:02.471
I wanna see some before I die.

12:06.726 --> 12:08.478
Aren't you in a lot of pain right now?

12:09.187 --> 12:11.772
This is about more than
just you living longer.

12:11.773 --> 12:13.857
Come on.
You're not dead yet.

12:13.858 --> 12:16.945
At least let them give you something
to ease the pain while you're still alive.

12:18.363 --> 12:20.156
Since when did you worry
about me like this?

12:21.616 --> 12:23.159
You were the one who ran off
to live your own life.

12:25.453 --> 12:29.081
And now that I'm dying,
you suddenly have a sense of duty?

12:29.082 --> 12:31.708
You're the one who needs to have
a sense of duty.

12:31.709 --> 12:35.213
What kind of mother wants to just die
and leave their kid by themself?

12:37.382 --> 12:38.675
Am I your mother?

12:39.550 --> 12:40.551
Well, aren't you?

12:41.386 --> 12:43.554
You gave birth to me.

12:48.351 --> 12:49.978
You think I had you
'cause I wanted to?

13:43.656 --> 13:49.579
WELCOME TO GOLD LAND
THE CITY OF DREAMS AND HOPES

13:56.878 --> 13:57.879
Hey.

14:01.132 --> 14:03.342
Yeah...

14:04.010 --> 14:07.262
What's this?
I expected a nice spread.

14:07.263 --> 14:10.223
Ah, come on.
Guess not.

14:10.224 --> 14:11.976
So disappointing.

14:13.352 --> 14:16.230
Anyway, I guess the chairman
isn't back from overseas.

14:17.273 --> 14:18.483
I must say, you're looking great.

14:19.817 --> 14:21.693
It must be fun playing
the chairman.

14:21.694 --> 14:23.487
Lee Dokyung's cell phone.

14:23.488 --> 14:25.197
Same guy you were tracking
a few days ago.

14:25.198 --> 14:27.574
- Does that mean he's dead?
-  No, he's in the hospital.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.659
But now the cops are on his tail.

14:29.660 --> 14:31.369
Hence our little meeting here.

14:31.370 --> 14:34.289
Not much I can do.
Not if the police are on him. No way.

14:34.290 --> 14:36.042
I'm not asking you to do anything
to Lee Dokyung.

14:37.668 --> 14:40.963
Just take this phone
and use it to find a person.

14:43.216 --> 14:45.051
No way he's working alone.

14:46.219 --> 14:47.220
He's got an accomplice.

14:48.179 --> 14:51.973
A stupid fuck who took off with
the van carrying all of our stuff.

14:53.976 --> 14:55.436
Ah, the casket.

14:56.312 --> 14:57.814
Ah, that must be a headache.

14:58.815 --> 15:02.609
Just dig through his calls and texts
and see what you can find.

15:02.610 --> 15:05.654
You can't expect me to do all that.
Come on.

15:05.655 --> 15:08.073
Searching through
a phone like that's illegal.

15:08.074 --> 15:09.534
And it takes too much time.

15:10.743 --> 15:13.120
Too much money, too.

15:13.121 --> 15:14.704
I'll give you the money,
so don't worry.

15:14.705 --> 15:15.956
Oh, yeah.

15:15.957 --> 15:17.415
Let me think about it, okay?

15:18.501 --> 15:19.710
There's no time for thinking.

15:20.878 --> 15:22.838
I gotta do this before
the chairman returns.

15:22.839 --> 15:24.590
And when is that?

15:25.633 --> 15:27.759
At the end of the month.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.095
I am curious, though.

15:29.804 --> 15:30.847
What's in the casket?

15:31.472 --> 15:32.639
Do you know?

15:32.640 --> 15:35.560
Drugs? Meth?

15:36.394 --> 15:37.811
Organs?

15:37.812 --> 15:41.022
Ah, you gangster assholes keep getting
into organ trafficking these days.

15:41.023 --> 15:42.107
You just can't help yourselves.

15:42.108 --> 15:43.818
Why the fuck do you need
to know everything?

15:45.069 --> 15:46.445
Just do what you usually do.

15:47.405 --> 15:49.157
Do what I'm telling you.

15:53.286 --> 15:54.871
Ah, hold on.

15:57.832 --> 16:01.878
Do I look like the kind of guy who
just does whatever you tell him to?

16:04.255 --> 16:05.798
Of course I'm that guy.

16:06.716 --> 16:07.799
Right.

16:09.468 --> 16:11.553
Fine, fine, I'll do it.

16:11.554 --> 16:12.555
Huh?

16:15.349 --> 16:17.934
Ah, dammit.
:cue

16:17.935 --> 16:20.937
GANGWON CENTRAL POLICE AGENCY

16:26.569 --> 16:29.321
Oh. Oh, there you are.

16:30.865 --> 16:32.658
- Here.
- Yeah.

16:38.998 --> 16:40.498
Read it, then shred it.

16:40.499 --> 16:43.043
You leave that lying around,
you'll get audited or somethin'.

16:43.044 --> 16:47.006
Oh. You think you're all that just 'cause
you're stationed at headquarters now?

16:48.716 --> 16:50.009
I'm your senior.

16:51.093 --> 16:52.135
ON-SITE INVESTIGATION REPORT

16:52.136 --> 16:53.220
It's a burner car.

16:53.221 --> 16:54.638
The plate number is fake, too.

16:54.639 --> 16:56.097
Dash cam?

16:56.098 --> 16:57.182
Nothin'.

16:57.183 --> 16:58.975
No surveillance cams in the area, either.

16:58.976 --> 17:00.353
So we don't know who the driver is.

17:01.729 --> 17:02.730
Why?

17:03.731 --> 17:05.065
The casket?

17:05.066 --> 17:06.566
Those Geumseong guys didn't take it?

17:06.567 --> 17:08.276
I don't think so.

17:08.277 --> 17:09.611
What does that mean?

17:09.612 --> 17:10.946
They either took it or they didn't.

17:10.947 --> 17:12.823
So why do you need all this?

17:13.991 --> 17:16.077
To keep Lee Dokyung quiet
in case he wants to talk?

17:16.786 --> 17:19.497
- Maybe.
- Uh, wait a minute.

17:20.081 --> 17:22.165
I'm not gonna be party to a murder.

17:22.166 --> 17:24.000
If that's the plan then I'm done.

17:24.001 --> 17:25.627
This is the last time I'm helping.

17:25.628 --> 17:27.963
You can tell Park
I'm not doing this anymore.

17:27.964 --> 17:31.174
And doing this will pay off my debts.

17:33.761 --> 17:34.762
Hey.

17:36.097 --> 17:37.806
How big of a hole are you in?

17:37.807 --> 17:39.684
100 million won?

17:40.643 --> 17:44.062
Oh, man, you really poured it down
the drain, didn't you?

17:45.898 --> 17:48.776
What do you like to play?
Baccarat?

17:49.694 --> 17:51.904
Ah, it won't be easy
to climb outta that hole.

17:54.657 --> 17:55.700
What about you?

17:56.325 --> 17:58.201
How much debt did you end up with?

17:58.202 --> 17:59.745
10 billion won?

18:00.913 --> 18:03.123
That's why you're still in this.
Ever since you were a patrol cop,

18:03.124 --> 18:05.083
you've been cleaning up shit
that Geumseong leaves for you, right?

18:05.084 --> 18:07.044
I paid them all back already.

18:07.670 --> 18:09.254
Oh, is that so?

18:09.255 --> 18:12.132
Well, if you're debt free then cleaning
up shit must be in your nature.

18:15.094 --> 18:16.929
You know what?

18:19.765 --> 18:21.600
You're a little shit.

18:21.601 --> 18:23.102
Better watch your mouth.

18:25.354 --> 18:26.689
Actually...

18:28.691 --> 18:29.859
My wife is very sick.

18:32.820 --> 18:34.071
That so?

18:37.158 --> 18:39.826
I'm going.
I don't want to see you again.

18:39.827 --> 18:41.828
Hey, hey, hey.

18:41.829 --> 18:45.332
At least tell me what's
in there before you go. Yeah?

18:45.333 --> 18:46.791
Whatever the hell it is,

18:46.792 --> 18:49.294
it's making the guys
at headquarters crazy.

18:49.295 --> 18:51.212
And yet Narcotics are being awfully quiet.

18:51.213 --> 18:52.756
So I guess it's not drugs.

18:52.757 --> 18:54.717
Park didn't tell you anything?

18:57.136 --> 18:58.470
Maybe he doesn't know.

18:58.471 --> 19:00.473
Then what is it?
Come on, just tell me.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.308
Huh?

19:03.643 --> 19:07.103
We got the information from Interpol
and it's still under review.

19:07.104 --> 19:08.563
You cannot leak this.

19:08.564 --> 19:10.274
All right, all right, prick.

19:14.236 --> 19:15.321
Gold bars.

19:18.115 --> 19:19.158
Gold bars?

19:21.410 --> 19:23.745
There's a Cambodian
trading company funded

19:23.746 --> 19:25.538
by the drug cartel, Krom thom.

19:25.539 --> 19:29.334
The word is that the chairman buried
a massive slush fund.

19:29.335 --> 19:31.504
Under the ground.
Like, actually buried it.

19:32.880 --> 19:34.798
Not cash, but gold bars.

19:34.799 --> 19:36.549
Ten tons worth.

19:36.550 --> 19:39.469
Somehow all
this information got leaked.

19:39.470 --> 19:41.054
And the government launched
a massive search

19:41.055 --> 19:42.889
and seizure for tax evasion.

19:42.890 --> 19:46.518
So all those gold bars,
they quickly moved them overseas.

19:46.519 --> 19:48.895
One ton of 10-kilogram gold bars
per shipment,

19:48.896 --> 19:51.148
disguised as caskets. However...

19:52.191 --> 19:53.776
...one was found
at the airport in Hong Kong.

19:54.360 --> 19:56.236
And apparently another one is in Korea.

19:56.237 --> 19:58.238
And that's the casket, huh?

19:58.239 --> 20:00.282
- The one with a ton of gold?
- Yeah, probably.

20:02.326 --> 20:03.493
And besides,

20:03.494 --> 20:06.330
that's the only casket that's come in
from Cambodia recently.

20:41.574 --> 20:45.035
SEONGOGAE REST AREA
:cue

20:58.841 --> 21:01.760
- Is anybody here?
-  Hi, there.

21:01.761 --> 21:03.928
- Yes, hello.
-  Ah, yes.

21:03.929 --> 21:07.015
Excuse me,
but the surveillance camera outside,

21:07.016 --> 21:08.184
did you install it?

21:08.934 --> 21:10.477
Yes.

21:10.478 --> 21:12.187
Well, I'm with the police. Here.

21:12.188 --> 21:13.605
I'm Detective Kim Jinman.

21:13.606 --> 21:16.941
I reported the installation of that camera
to the police already.

21:16.942 --> 21:18.234
Might there be an issue?

21:18.235 --> 21:20.111
Oh, no, no.
It's nothing like that.

21:20.112 --> 21:22.614
There was a traffic accident out front
a few days ago.

21:22.615 --> 21:24.575
- I just want to check something out. Yeah.
-  I see.

21:35.169 --> 21:36.503
GANGWON CENTRAL POLICE AGENCY
TRAFFIC INFORMATION CENTER

21:36.504 --> 21:37.879
- One moment. I'll take a look.
-  Yeah.

21:37.880 --> 21:39.839
Okay.

21:39.840 --> 21:43.051
12:29 A.M.
Jingogae Intersection.

21:43.052 --> 21:46.846
And at 12:57 A.M.,
21 Jinbu Street.

21:46.847 --> 21:50.934
Next, at 1:32 A.M.
National Route 59.

21:50.935 --> 21:52.435
And at 1:55 A.M.,

21:52.436 --> 21:54.021
crossing Jeongsan Bridge.

21:54.939 --> 21:56.023
Jeongsan?

21:57.107 --> 21:58.317
Yes.

21:59.401 --> 22:00.944
GEUMSEONG TOURIST HOTEL

22:00.945 --> 22:06.699
♪ I'm begging you please
Don't cling to me anymore ♪

22:06.700 --> 22:08.368
♪ Don't come looking for me ♪

22:08.369 --> 22:09.702
Stop it.

22:09.703 --> 22:12.580
Ah, honey, it's fine.

22:12.581 --> 22:14.958
Wow, what's up with your hands?

22:14.959 --> 22:16.501
They're so pretty for a man.

22:16.502 --> 22:18.086
Because they're woman's hands.

22:18.087 --> 22:20.004
That means it's fine if I touch you, right?

22:20.005 --> 22:21.548
Just kidding!

22:21.549 --> 22:25.468
♪ A heartless girl
when I'm already breaking inside ♪

22:25.469 --> 22:27.011
Park Hocheol's here!

22:27.012 --> 22:28.930
♪ So now just for a while... ♪

22:28.931 --> 22:29.931
CANCEL

22:29.932 --> 22:31.015
-  Hey.
- What?

22:31.016 --> 22:32.642
- I finally found my love today!
- Get him outta here.

22:32.643 --> 22:34.352
- It's no fair!
- I know, I know.

22:34.353 --> 22:35.687
Oh, honey.

22:35.688 --> 22:38.398
You know, right?
My love?

22:38.399 --> 22:40.900
Honey, I have to be really honest
with you.

22:40.901 --> 22:42.569
Jeongah.

22:42.570 --> 22:43.779
Sorry!

22:44.655 --> 22:46.322
Oh, look.
Park has arrived.

22:46.323 --> 22:48.741
Right when we're getting
this party started.

22:50.035 --> 22:52.287
I'm taking two of those girls out with me.

22:52.288 --> 22:55.081
- Have you found anything?
-  Of course I did!

22:55.082 --> 22:56.584
Wait, what did I...

22:57.501 --> 22:59.003
You talkin' about the van?

22:59.670 --> 23:01.713
Yeah, I've been looking around for it.

23:01.714 --> 23:04.173
I combed through the surveillance cameras
in Gangwon-do.

23:04.174 --> 23:05.592
I checked every single one.

23:05.593 --> 23:07.136
Quit rambling and just spit it out.

23:08.721 --> 23:09.804
Hey.

23:09.805 --> 23:11.891
I'm taking two of them today.

23:12.433 --> 23:14.100
- Yes, sir.
-  Yeah? You got it?

23:14.101 --> 23:15.226
-  Huh?
-  Hey.

23:15.227 --> 23:16.811
- Move it.
-  Yeah.

23:16.812 --> 23:18.688
Yeah, go get-
what are you doing?

23:18.689 --> 23:21.025
Go. Get them ready.
Good.

23:22.359 --> 23:23.860
Ah.

23:23.861 --> 23:25.446
What was I saying?

23:26.614 --> 23:28.073
Oh, right. The van.

23:28.991 --> 23:33.369
Was last seen here in Jeongsan.
Where we are.

23:33.370 --> 23:36.205
It was caught
on surveillance cameras.

23:36.206 --> 23:39.542
It shows up at the entrance
to Jeongsan Bridge.

23:39.543 --> 23:41.044
Then no trace of it anywhere.

23:41.045 --> 23:42.503
And two days later,

23:42.504 --> 23:45.715
they dump the van
at the abandoned warehouse,

23:45.716 --> 23:47.176
but it was empty.

23:47.927 --> 23:50.887
So where did they hide
the casket? Huh?

23:52.389 --> 23:54.223
Right here.

23:54.224 --> 23:55.850
Jeongsan.

23:55.851 --> 23:58.061
They hid it here.

23:58.062 --> 24:00.730
So who was it, then?
The prick who was driving it?

24:00.731 --> 24:02.607
Oh, I don't really know about that.

24:02.608 --> 24:06.569
But either way, I've really
helped you narrow it down.

24:06.570 --> 24:09.698
Just find out who was in Jeongsan that day
and catch 'em.

24:10.699 --> 24:11.783
Wouldn't that work?

24:11.784 --> 24:12.785
Find out quickly.

24:14.578 --> 24:17.414
Right, but I think I got a hold
of some info that you're gonna wanna hear.

24:18.207 --> 24:19.958
Yeah. You should know.

24:19.959 --> 24:21.960
-  Yeah?
- What?

24:21.961 --> 24:24.963
I'm guessing you don't know what's in
that casket, do you?

24:24.964 --> 24:26.006
Well?

24:29.093 --> 24:31.553
You don't know, huh?
Well, I do.

24:36.225 --> 24:37.850
What's in it?

24:37.851 --> 24:41.020
Well, this info's worth
at least 100 gold chips.

24:41.021 --> 24:42.606
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
We can do that.

24:44.817 --> 24:46.652
Gold bars.

24:48.654 --> 24:50.280
A ton of them.

24:51.115 --> 24:52.449
One ton.

24:53.367 --> 24:54.618
The current market value...

24:56.245 --> 24:57.704
150 billion.

24:57.705 --> 24:59.498
Crazy, right?

25:00.582 --> 25:03.459
But then again,
you know what's really crazy?

25:03.460 --> 25:09.382
Is that, well, the chairman didn't
tell you you'd be smuggling gold, huh?

25:09.383 --> 25:10.801
Why is that?

25:11.552 --> 25:13.929
Seems like the kind of important stuff
you should know.

25:16.306 --> 25:18.975
I mean,
you are his right-hand man.

25:18.976 --> 25:20.768
Does that mean...

25:20.769 --> 25:22.604
...is he demoting you?

25:24.356 --> 25:26.400
Guess it doesn't matter.

25:27.151 --> 25:28.610
As long as you get the job done.
:cue

25:34.283 --> 25:36.492
Yeah. So.

25:36.493 --> 25:39.038
I heard that you're one
of the best goldsmiths in the area.

25:40.080 --> 25:43.249
Uh, yes, well...

25:43.250 --> 25:45.710
- You've manufactured gold bars yourself?
-  Yes.

25:45.711 --> 25:48.129
I need you to make ten bars.

25:48.130 --> 25:50.381
One kilo each, just like
I said on the phone.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.051
And of course we'll provide the gold.

25:53.093 --> 25:54.302
And your casting fee?

25:54.303 --> 25:55.429
Mm...

25:57.598 --> 25:58.890
One percent of cost.

25:58.891 --> 26:00.975
Pretty good, right?

26:00.976 --> 26:03.145
It's not every day you get
an offer like this.

26:04.396 --> 26:06.857
I'm curious,
how long will it take to make them?

26:07.816 --> 26:09.525
Around two to three days.

26:09.526 --> 26:11.319
- Two to three.
-  You see,

26:11.320 --> 26:12.278
gold bars don't require...

26:14.948 --> 26:16.658
Detailed craftsmanship.

26:17.242 --> 26:18.326
One thing, though.

26:18.327 --> 26:20.788
Where in Jeongsan are you from, exactly?

26:21.705 --> 26:23.790
Don't you have a business card?

26:23.791 --> 26:25.666
It's just that normally gold bars

26:25.667 --> 26:28.544
are manufactured
in specific authorized factories,

26:28.545 --> 26:29.837
so why don't you go to those?

26:29.838 --> 26:31.298
The thing is...

26:32.800 --> 26:34.843
There's a reason why I'm paying you such
a high fee.

26:36.220 --> 26:37.554
It comes with one condition.

26:38.597 --> 26:39.889
What condition, you ask?

26:39.890 --> 26:41.390
No questions.

26:41.391 --> 26:44.769
The who, what, why, where,
none of it.

26:44.770 --> 26:46.896
They say silence is golden, right?

26:46.897 --> 26:50.900
So stay silent
and you can call it a golden fee.

26:50.901 --> 26:52.610
A golden fee?

26:52.611 --> 26:53.945
Yeah, that's right.

26:53.946 --> 26:55.780
And there's a second condition.

26:55.781 --> 26:57.156
It's not just questions.

26:57.157 --> 26:58.741
You can't say anything.

26:58.742 --> 26:59.826
You can't go around saying,

26:59.827 --> 27:02.578
"Hey, I'm working on this gold job.
They're 10-kilo bars,"

27:02.579 --> 27:04.539
to literally anyone.
If you do,

27:04.540 --> 27:06.124
our contract is over.

27:06.125 --> 27:08.918
Not only that,
your life will be over.

27:08.919 --> 27:10.254
Then you bought them illegally.

27:11.255 --> 27:12.548
If I refuse now...

27:13.465 --> 27:14.925
...I'll be okay, right?

27:18.095 --> 27:19.470
Of course.

27:19.471 --> 27:23.474
Mm, it's not like you saw
the gold or anything.

27:23.475 --> 27:25.142
So yeah,
if you don't wanna do it,

27:25.143 --> 27:27.353
no biggie.
It's not like anyone saw us here.

27:27.354 --> 27:31.775
No one knows that we met to talk and-
two percent, okay?

27:33.277 --> 27:34.486
3K per kilo.

27:35.362 --> 27:37.530
300 million for ten bars.

27:37.531 --> 27:39.032
Do you know anyone
who makes that in a month?

27:39.950 --> 27:42.326
I wouldn't offer this to anybody else,
Hoonseok.

27:42.327 --> 27:44.287
I like your face.

27:44.288 --> 27:47.540
You look like the type of guy
who'd make gold bars with total precision.

27:47.541 --> 27:49.126
I really want to work with you, okay?

27:51.211 --> 27:52.879
But if you'd rather refuse, say so, hmm?

27:52.880 --> 27:54.922
I'm a busy man.
I have to go look for someone else now.

27:54.923 --> 27:57.593
- We're done here.
-  The gold bar.

27:58.635 --> 28:01.096
Show me.
Then I'll decide.

28:03.348 --> 28:04.349
Okay.

28:09.938 --> 28:12.648
Here. This is it.

28:12.649 --> 28:13.775
Okay.

28:21.241 --> 28:22.909
Here he is.

28:22.910 --> 28:24.286
Mr. Lee Hoonseok.

28:25.787 --> 28:27.121
Yeah.

28:27.122 --> 28:28.916
And this is, uh...

28:30.042 --> 28:31.126
Call her Boss.

28:32.544 --> 28:34.963
Nice to meet you, Boss.

28:36.089 --> 28:37.466
Hello.

28:37.883 --> 28:39.216
He's going to work with us.

28:39.217 --> 28:40.552
He'll make the...

28:42.554 --> 28:44.388
You know what?
I've noticed your voice is kind of loud,

28:44.389 --> 28:46.475
so from now on we'll call
the gold bars "potatoes," okay?

28:47.225 --> 28:48.310
Show him the potato.

28:49.561 --> 28:51.229
He wants to check it.
:cue

28:54.775 --> 28:56.318
Hey, it's okay.
You're good to show him.

28:58.028 --> 28:59.655
We're all in the same boat now
so it's cool.

29:09.706 --> 29:11.332
Here.

29:32.729 --> 29:34.523
This is real.

29:35.899 --> 29:37.901
Well, of course it is.
It's the real deal.

29:40.153 --> 29:41.737
All right, I'll have it done.

29:41.738 --> 29:43.531
It won't take long.
Come back tomorrow night.

29:43.532 --> 29:45.033
Uh, no, no, no.

29:46.493 --> 29:47.576
It'd be better...

29:49.663 --> 29:50.913
...if you could start work today.

29:50.914 --> 29:52.498
And I would like to supervise.

29:52.499 --> 29:55.293
That's right. And while she's watching,
I'll also be watching.

29:56.837 --> 29:58.462
I can't do it right away.

29:58.463 --> 30:01.298
I need to get things like
a new crucible and new molds,

30:01.299 --> 30:02.800
and if we're stamping
the Korea Mint mark...

30:02.801 --> 30:03.844
I can wait.

30:04.761 --> 30:06.554
Yeah, yeah.
We can wait.

30:06.555 --> 30:09.098
Hey, you can understand
why she's suspicious.

30:09.099 --> 30:11.058
You can get all those things today, right?

30:11.059 --> 30:13.185
Then we can get started tonight, huh?

30:13.186 --> 30:14.312
Pull an all-nighter?

30:16.648 --> 30:17.983
How about this?

30:19.234 --> 30:20.360
Midnight tonight.

30:21.278 --> 30:22.863
Come to the front of the workshop.

30:24.823 --> 30:26.365
When everything's all set,
I'll give you guys a call.

30:26.366 --> 30:27.825
- And I'll let you inside.
-  Nice.

30:27.826 --> 30:29.118
All right.

30:29.119 --> 30:30.120
So I'll call you later.

30:31.913 --> 30:33.706
- See you at midnight.
- Mm-hmm.

30:33.707 --> 30:35.667
Call us. Call us later.

30:41.673 --> 30:42.965
See?

30:42.966 --> 30:44.383
What'd I say?

30:44.384 --> 30:46.093
There's nothing money can't buy.

30:46.094 --> 30:49.263
Do you really think he's the right guy?

30:49.264 --> 30:50.599
He seems too nice.

30:51.892 --> 30:53.225
So? What's wrong with being a nice guy?

30:53.226 --> 30:54.560
He could have a sudden change
of heart

30:54.561 --> 30:57.605
and decide to report us to the police.

30:57.606 --> 30:59.148
Stop worrying about that.

30:59.149 --> 31:01.026
I told you I did
a background check on the guy.

31:01.943 --> 31:03.278
That guy there?

31:04.196 --> 31:06.280
He lives with his widowed mother
and sister.

31:06.281 --> 31:08.240
He's the breadwinner of the family.

31:08.241 --> 31:09.493
So what?

31:10.619 --> 31:11.953
Heeju.

31:12.788 --> 31:15.206
This is how we make deals in my world, okay?

31:15.207 --> 31:17.208
Money's important
but collateral's necessary.

31:17.209 --> 31:18.584
It's absolutely essential.

31:18.585 --> 31:21.128
Last thing you want
is to get stabbed in the back.

31:21.129 --> 31:23.464
So you always have to consider
the worst-case scenario.

31:23.465 --> 31:24.965
And these guys?

31:24.966 --> 31:28.010
What's the one thing that keeps them
from doing something stupid or crazy?

31:28.011 --> 31:29.845
Collateral, of course.

31:29.846 --> 31:31.472
The more important the collateral is,

31:31.473 --> 31:33.183
the less likely they are
to screw us over.

31:34.643 --> 31:35.894
So you're saying...

31:37.062 --> 31:40.398
...his mom and younger sister
are collateral?

31:43.110 --> 31:45.903
- Ah, come on. You know what I mean.
-  Then what's my collateral?

31:45.904 --> 31:47.364
Is it my aunt?

31:49.449 --> 31:50.533
Heeju.

31:50.534 --> 31:51.992
That's why you went to the pawn shop
the other day.

31:51.993 --> 31:53.452
To check on my collateral?

31:53.453 --> 31:55.204
Are you seriously asking me that?

31:55.205 --> 31:56.872
I went because I wanted to see Auntie.

31:56.873 --> 31:59.667
You got it all wrong.
It's not like that.

31:59.668 --> 32:01.043
Ah, come on.

32:01.044 --> 32:02.419
Collateral's insane.

32:02.420 --> 32:04.547
How 'bout we go eat?
What do you want?

32:06.007 --> 32:07.259
Bokjiri sounds good...
:cue

32:13.098 --> 32:14.349
Something's wrong.

32:15.642 --> 32:16.892
Give him a call.

32:16.893 --> 32:18.269
Well, he said he'd call
when he's ready.

32:23.316 --> 32:24.317
Yeah?

32:25.694 --> 32:26.736
Mm, okay.

32:59.895 --> 33:02.563
JEIL WORKSHOP

33:21.875 --> 33:23.292
Oh, here.

33:23.293 --> 33:24.419
Oh.

33:32.928 --> 33:34.845
I got it.

33:34.846 --> 33:36.096
Here.

33:43.271 --> 33:44.897
How long will it take?

33:44.898 --> 33:47.483
I'll be done with it before morning.

33:47.484 --> 33:50.278
I guess you two just wait here.

33:52.113 --> 33:55.199
Yeah, and don't you even think
about pulling any stunts.

33:55.200 --> 33:56.993
I'll be watching you.

33:58.119 --> 33:59.954
I'm watching you over there, too!

35:10.025 --> 35:13.652
INCOMING CALL
JEIL WORKSHOP PRESIDENT NOH

35:13.653 --> 35:16.739
JEWELRY ECONOMY DAILY

35:21.328 --> 35:22.454
That's right.

35:27.626 --> 35:29.753
You went into that coal mine.

35:34.466 --> 35:35.925
DAD! BE SAFE AGAIN TODAY

35:48.813 --> 35:50.023
You were there?

35:50.982 --> 35:53.652
Of course I was.

36:00.408 --> 36:01.534
What was the name of that mutt, again?

36:02.994 --> 36:04.746
Mongsil or something.

36:05.955 --> 36:07.331
Don't you remember?

36:07.332 --> 36:09.125
You went in there while we
were playing freeze tag, I think.

36:11.211 --> 36:12.920
You were looking
for that stupid dog

36:12.921 --> 36:14.672
and I waited for you forever.

36:16.049 --> 36:18.425
I kept waiting,
but you didn't come out.

36:18.426 --> 36:20.762
So I went to get the Aunties.

36:23.014 --> 36:25.099
Mongsil, wait!
:cue

36:26.976 --> 36:28.436
Mongsil!

36:32.941 --> 36:34.192
Mongsil!

36:37.028 --> 36:38.863
Mongsil, here!

36:48.206 --> 36:49.541
Mongsil!

36:52.669 --> 36:53.878
Heeju.

36:56.214 --> 36:57.298
You don't remember?

37:00.468 --> 37:03.471
I'm not sure.
I don't think so.

37:05.557 --> 37:07.267
You really forgot.

37:08.351 --> 37:10.686
Come on.
You gotta remember.

37:10.687 --> 37:12.897
I practically saved your life, you know?

37:13.773 --> 37:14.857
I don't know.

37:14.858 --> 37:16.359
I seriously don't remember.

37:50.477 --> 37:52.311
Hoonseok?

37:54.189 --> 37:56.524
-  Shh, quiet. Quiet.
-  Are you there?

37:57.358 --> 37:58.359
Who is it?

37:59.736 --> 38:01.236
Hey! What are you doing?

38:01.237 --> 38:03.822
It's-it's the owner.

38:05.533 --> 38:06.701
Hold on.

38:09.871 --> 38:11.206
Hoonseok!

38:13.082 --> 38:14.374
Quick, come on.

38:14.375 --> 38:15.876
- Come on.
-  Are you asleep?

38:20.507 --> 38:22.216
Hoonseok.

38:25.470 --> 38:26.845
Ah, goodness.

38:26.846 --> 38:29.056
So you were in here.

38:29.057 --> 38:30.474
Yes. What are you...

38:30.475 --> 38:32.601
Well, why did you lock the door?

38:32.602 --> 38:34.479
What are you doing up at this hour?

38:36.940 --> 38:38.608
Uh, sir, can I talk to you for a sec?

38:40.610 --> 38:41.611
Hold on.

38:44.113 --> 38:47.033
There's nothing...

38:48.618 --> 38:49.661
Sir?

38:51.996 --> 38:53.747
Wait.

38:53.748 --> 38:55.750
What-what's all that?

38:58.795 --> 39:01.046
Spit it out!

39:01.047 --> 39:02.340
What are you up to?

39:03.341 --> 39:05.884
Someone from Janggak asked me
to do some craft work.

39:05.885 --> 39:07.344
Let go.

39:08.429 --> 39:10.764
What? Seems like a lot.

39:10.765 --> 39:13.601
It's 14k.
There's not much gold in it.

39:14.978 --> 39:16.228
Hold on, sir!

39:16.229 --> 39:17.187
Why do you wanna go in there?

39:17.188 --> 39:19.481
There's nothing to...

39:19.482 --> 39:20.899
Goodness, what's with you?

39:26.364 --> 39:27.990
What are you doing at this hour?

39:27.991 --> 39:29.200
Why aren't you at home sleeping?

39:34.289 --> 39:35.789
I couldn't sleep.

39:39.043 --> 39:41.838
I decided to sell this factory
to President Choi.

39:42.797 --> 39:44.215
It's best you stop working here...

39:45.967 --> 39:47.426
...and look somewhere else.

39:47.427 --> 39:48.595
But sir...

39:49.596 --> 39:51.055
I'm very sorry.

39:51.764 --> 39:53.641
I wanted to help you send your sister
to college.

39:54.559 --> 39:56.727
And of course I wanted to help your mom.

39:56.728 --> 39:59.439
Make sure you could take care
of her while she's unwell.

40:00.148 --> 40:02.817
But there's just
no way I can hold on anymore.

40:04.819 --> 40:06.528
Forget about me.

40:06.529 --> 40:09.239
What are you going
to do about paying off your loan?

40:09.240 --> 40:12.326
I thought you said Mr. Choi's offer
wasn't that great.

40:12.327 --> 40:15.037
Look, I wasn't good enough.

40:15.038 --> 40:17.164
That's why I'm in debt.
What can you do?

40:17.165 --> 40:18.875
Okay.

40:20.376 --> 40:21.627
Be careful.

40:21.628 --> 40:24.547
I hear there are a lot
of thieves stealing gold dust.

40:25.256 --> 40:27.090
Better keep the doors locked up.

40:27.091 --> 40:28.425
Yeah.

40:28.426 --> 40:30.344
Thank you.

40:30.345 --> 40:32.804
You've always been a hard worker.

40:37.352 --> 40:38.353
:cue

40:47.445 --> 40:49.113
Wait a minute.
What was that noise?

40:49.989 --> 40:52.366
Uh, what noise?
I didn't hear any noise.

40:52.367 --> 40:54.368
- What's wrong with you?
-  Nothing.

40:54.369 --> 40:55.452
Get out of my way, kid!

40:55.453 --> 40:57.663
-  What was that?
-  That was nothing!

40:57.664 --> 41:00.040
-  You should just go...
- I'm going in!

41:00.041 --> 41:02.377
Sir, wait, please!
Don't go in there!

41:09.550 --> 41:11.385
We're fucked.
We're so fucked.

41:11.386 --> 41:12.553
Sir, are you okay?

41:14.013 --> 41:16.181
Why'd you do that?

41:16.182 --> 41:18.685
Sir, are you okay?

41:20.019 --> 41:21.604
He needs to go to the hospital.

41:23.564 --> 41:25.400
We have to take him, okay?

41:27.235 --> 41:29.361
Woogy. Hey. Hey!

41:29.362 --> 41:30.613
What are you doing?

41:31.447 --> 41:32.531
We have no choice.

41:32.532 --> 41:34.074
He saw the gold bar
so I gotta finish him off.

41:34.075 --> 41:35.117
- No!
-  Are you crazy?

41:35.118 --> 41:36.952
Let go.

41:36.953 --> 41:38.120
Let go!

41:38.121 --> 41:40.288
Wait! Wait a second!

41:40.289 --> 41:42.124
Just-just put that down, okay?

41:42.125 --> 41:43.751
If you don't wanna help,
get out of the way.

41:44.669 --> 41:46.545
-  I gotta cut him into pieces.
- No! You can't do that, no!

41:46.546 --> 41:47.838
Cut him up?

41:47.839 --> 41:49.715
- He's alive still!
-  Is he?

41:49.716 --> 41:51.591
I guess I just have to kill him, then!

41:51.592 --> 41:52.718
You want the gold?

41:52.719 --> 41:54.136
Then fucking move!

41:54.137 --> 41:55.804
- No, you can't! You can't!
-  Get off!

41:55.805 --> 41:57.764
I can talk to him!

41:57.765 --> 41:59.474
I can say you were thieves!
He won't know about the gold!

41:59.475 --> 42:01.768
Yeah! L-let him take him
to the hospital.

42:01.769 --> 42:03.729
After that, we can let
Hoonseok take care of it.

42:03.730 --> 42:05.313
Enough. Move out of the way.

42:07.108 --> 42:10.193
If you kill my boss,
then you'll have to kill me, too!

42:10.194 --> 42:11.570
Or else I'll spill everything I know!

42:11.571 --> 42:13.447
If you do this,

42:13.448 --> 42:16.241
then you and I are through!
You gonna kill me as well?

42:18.828 --> 42:21.831
Woogy. Woogy, please.

42:23.249 --> 42:24.791
You always used to listen to me.

42:24.792 --> 42:26.669
When we were kids.

42:28.671 --> 42:29.755
At the coal mine.

42:29.756 --> 42:31.382
And I fell down.

42:32.175 --> 42:34.385
It was you who saved me, right?

42:37.138 --> 42:38.681
That's right.

42:39.599 --> 42:41.433
I remember.

42:41.434 --> 42:42.477
It's just...

42:44.353 --> 42:45.688
...I didn't wanna remember it.

42:53.654 --> 42:55.030
Fuck.

43:11.339 --> 43:13.882
- Whoa, no!
-  Hey! What?

43:13.883 --> 43:15.009
We're taking him to the hospital, right?

43:15.843 --> 43:19.639
Wait, wait, wait!
Behind your back, you-you have a knife.

43:20.723 --> 43:22.725
Fuck.

43:31.943 --> 43:35.403
Ah, fuck these damn
conscientious assholes.

43:38.032 --> 43:39.492
Oh, what the fuck am I doing?

43:42.954 --> 43:44.163
Is this even right?

43:44.789 --> 43:48.708
Ah, what is this shit? Ah!

44:22.660 --> 44:24.453
:cue

44:42.013 --> 44:43.889
Okay.

44:43.890 --> 44:46.808
If they're off by point-one gram,
there's no need to worry.

44:46.809 --> 44:51.104
That's within the normal weight range,
so you'll sell them without any issues.

44:51.105 --> 44:54.316
As for the leftover dust and fragments,
I'll keep them here,

44:54.317 --> 44:56.526
and I'll mix them in when I do
the next casting.

44:57.778 --> 44:59.488
Thank you so much.
You did good work.

45:00.573 --> 45:02.073
Nice work.

45:02.074 --> 45:03.867
I'll be back in three days, 'kay?

45:03.868 --> 45:05.286
And the cash?

45:06.078 --> 45:07.205
Didn't we tell you?

45:08.664 --> 45:09.748
You didn't tell him?

45:09.749 --> 45:11.209
What?

45:12.251 --> 45:14.044
Well, it's a deferred payment.

45:14.045 --> 45:15.754
I'll settle it in three days.

45:15.755 --> 45:17.255
Wait, wait, wait.
Wait a minute.

45:17.256 --> 45:18.465
Uh, deferred?

45:18.466 --> 45:20.301
Come on.

45:21.219 --> 45:22.469
Shit, you don't trust us?

45:22.470 --> 45:24.429
Of course I don't trust you!

45:24.430 --> 45:27.557
How do I know you two will actually
come back in three days?

45:27.558 --> 45:29.184
Well, what do you want?

45:29.185 --> 45:30.518
I don't have it!
I don't have the cash!

45:30.519 --> 45:33.813
Hold on. We-we agreed
to give you two percent, didn't we?

45:33.814 --> 45:34.982
Yeah.

45:36.692 --> 45:37.776
Well, this...

45:39.153 --> 45:41.321
...is worth 150 mil.

45:41.322 --> 45:43.323
Consider this half upfront.

45:43.324 --> 45:46.077
And you'll get the rest once
the job is done.

45:46.994 --> 45:47.995
Oh.

45:49.956 --> 45:53.167
Wow. You really scored.

45:53.918 --> 45:55.211
Lucky you.

45:55.920 --> 45:58.129
Give it to me.
I'll exchange it for you.

45:58.130 --> 46:01.175
No, thanks.
I can take care of it myself.

46:02.385 --> 46:05.846
And you'll promise us that you'll be able
to work on the rest, too?

46:07.098 --> 46:09.808
Yes, Boss.
I'll do it because I trust you.

46:11.727 --> 46:14.020
But I don't trust him at all.

46:14.021 --> 46:17.816
You motherfucker. You think you can point
your finger and say that shit to my face?

46:17.817 --> 46:19.359
Who the fuck do you think you are?

46:19.360 --> 46:20.527
- You wanna die?
- See you next time.

46:20.528 --> 46:22.362
What a piece of shit.
Hey, hey!

46:22.363 --> 46:24.239
I don't trust you either, you
prick!

46:24.240 --> 46:26.742
-  Where's my knife? No!
-  Stop it. Come on. Come on.

46:35.084 --> 46:36.085
Sorry.

46:37.211 --> 46:39.088
I got worked up earlier.

46:40.715 --> 46:43.050
The whole situation kinda got out
of control.

46:46.345 --> 46:47.596
Do you need a doctor?

46:48.472 --> 46:49.473
Forget it.

46:50.391 --> 46:52.435
Instead, I need your word.

46:53.269 --> 46:57.147
If you and I are going to work together,
you won't kill anyone.

46:57.148 --> 47:01.318
If you ever pull a knife
or spill blood one more time,

47:01.319 --> 47:03.112
you and I are done.
It's over.

47:07.366 --> 47:09.368
What if someone finds out
we're doing this?

47:14.332 --> 47:16.875
You think you're being
fucking conscientious?

47:16.876 --> 47:17.877
Hmm?

47:20.421 --> 47:22.339
That mindset doesn't make
any fucking sense

47:22.340 --> 47:23.466
for a wannabe thief.

47:24.383 --> 47:28.011
Fuck.
You're stealing gold, you know.

47:28.012 --> 47:30.556
A whopping 100 kilograms
of someone else's gold.

47:31.265 --> 47:34.559
And now you want the money?
All in good conscience?

47:34.560 --> 47:36.395
Without getting blood
on your hands?

47:41.901 --> 47:43.693
Well, then.

47:43.694 --> 47:45.404
Do you promise or not?

47:48.741 --> 47:50.325
Yeah, I'll do my best.

47:59.168 --> 48:00.169
Here.
:cue

48:52.888 --> 48:54.597
How much longer
are you gonna sleep?

48:54.598 --> 48:56.434
It's already dark out.

48:57.476 --> 48:58.894
Keep still.

49:00.312 --> 49:01.313
Almost done.

49:15.911 --> 49:16.912
Go.

49:18.664 --> 49:20.040
Get out of here.

49:22.084 --> 49:23.418
Run away.

49:23.419 --> 49:25.254
I'll pay off all of your debt for you.

49:26.172 --> 49:28.757
Do you even have the money
to pay off my debt?

49:29.383 --> 49:30.593
You don't even know what I owe.

49:31.677 --> 49:33.219
How much is it?

49:36.182 --> 49:37.475
I don't have debt.

49:38.934 --> 49:41.020
When it's time, I'll leave quietly.
Don't worry.

49:42.021 --> 49:43.063
Where were you last night?

49:45.191 --> 49:46.817
Were you hanging out with that thug?

49:48.110 --> 49:50.236
- What on Earth did you do with your hand?
- I already told you,

49:50.237 --> 49:51.614
there's nothing going on!

49:52.990 --> 49:54.074
And my hand...

49:55.284 --> 49:56.826
I just fell, okay?

49:56.827 --> 49:58.870
Don't tell me it was from a fall!
It was from a knife.

49:58.871 --> 50:00.206
Enough, all right.

50:01.123 --> 50:03.750
Wow. You luckless bitch.

50:04.877 --> 50:06.962
You ran away and still ended up like this.

50:11.550 --> 50:13.594
You wanna know what's really ridiculous?

50:14.637 --> 50:18.516
Everyone can tell that the bitch
with the worst luck is you.

50:19.892 --> 50:22.603
So hearing you call me that
just makes me furious.

50:23.646 --> 50:25.231
It really pisses me off.

50:28.526 --> 50:30.528
Don't put all your trust
into men like that.

50:32.154 --> 50:34.155
One moment can ruin your whole life.

50:34.156 --> 50:35.657
You're one to talk.

50:35.658 --> 50:37.992
Then why did you marry that trash?

50:37.993 --> 50:39.702
To survive.

50:39.703 --> 50:42.205
You think I could pay off my debt
and raise a kid by serving coffee?

50:42.206 --> 50:44.499
- If it weren't for you I would've...
-  Don't use me as an excuse!

50:44.500 --> 50:46.252
I never asked for any of that!

50:47.711 --> 50:50.046
Every single moment I had to spend
with that man was nothing but hell!

50:50.047 --> 50:51.214
An do you think I was happy?

50:51.215 --> 50:53.967
That's why I begged you to run away!

50:53.968 --> 50:55.301
You didn't wanna go, though!

50:55.302 --> 50:57.554
Even after I told you what
that man tried to do to me, you...

50:57.555 --> 50:59.806
What is the point
of dredging this up now?

50:59.807 --> 51:01.432
Should I beg for your forgiveness?

51:01.433 --> 51:02.977
- Would that make it better?
-  Yes!

51:03.894 --> 51:05.478
Beg and apologize.

51:05.479 --> 51:07.146
So I can feel better.

51:51.567 --> 51:53.192
Heeju, Heeju.
Don't come out.

51:53.193 --> 51:54.612
Your uncle is here.

52:05.205 --> 52:07.373
Well? You glad to see me?

52:07.374 --> 52:08.875
It's been two months.

52:08.876 --> 52:12.254
Uh, I was about to close up here.

52:13.547 --> 52:15.841
Let's go home.
Did you eat?

52:21.764 --> 52:23.015
Get in here already.

52:26.226 --> 52:29.395
Hi. It's me again.

52:29.396 --> 52:31.482
:cue

52:33.817 --> 52:37.820
So I heard you sold a watch
to Mr. Jang a week ago.

52:37.821 --> 52:39.615
For 30 million.

52:40.866 --> 52:42.868
How much did you pay for it?

52:43.786 --> 52:45.745
You were able to sell for a high price.

52:45.746 --> 52:47.372
And you didn't tell me.

52:49.291 --> 52:54.128
I mean, I thought the price was, well,
a little too high.

52:54.129 --> 52:55.631
So I let Han know.

52:56.715 --> 52:58.050
All right, bring me the ledger.

52:59.176 --> 53:02.261
I said bring me the ledger.

53:22.408 --> 53:24.076
What else did you say you took?

53:24.868 --> 53:27.453
That's all for this month.
Wait, actually,

53:27.454 --> 53:29.497
I bought a few rings, too.

53:29.498 --> 53:31.457
I think she priced those correctly.

53:33.794 --> 53:35.545
You said you got diamonds.

53:35.546 --> 53:37.756
'Bout a month ago.

53:43.011 --> 53:44.054
No diamonds.

53:45.097 --> 53:47.015
Not even one.

53:52.229 --> 53:54.648
Is there a separate ledger for Janggak?

54:05.033 --> 54:06.326
You can go home now.

54:09.121 --> 54:12.331
I hope I didn't say anything that
was unnecessary.

54:12.332 --> 54:14.500
No, you were right to.

54:14.501 --> 54:16.545
I'm the owner and the husband.

54:17.212 --> 54:19.130
- Best that I know everything.
- Right.

54:19.131 --> 54:21.299
All right, then.
Take care.

54:23.469 --> 54:25.094
Uh, I'll see you.

54:25.095 --> 54:26.221
Goodbye.

54:39.401 --> 54:41.570
You must
have really lost your mind.

54:45.115 --> 54:48.409
You were just a coffee shop girl
with a little kid.

54:48.410 --> 54:50.411
I took you in and fed you,

54:50.412 --> 54:53.039
and you thank me
by taking my money on the sly?

55:02.758 --> 55:04.134
When did this start?

55:06.261 --> 55:08.055
How much have you skimmed now?

55:10.933 --> 55:12.726
- That's all.
-  Oh.

55:13.852 --> 55:15.521
Really?

55:17.356 --> 55:20.567
You thieving bitch.

55:21.318 --> 55:24.278
Look at you still lying through
your fucking teeth!

55:30.369 --> 55:31.411
Shit!

55:35.040 --> 55:36.123
Where do you think you're going?

55:36.124 --> 55:37.625
Come here!

55:45.592 --> 55:47.802
Better not say you fucking spent it all.

55:47.803 --> 55:51.098
If you did, I swear I'll
send you straight to Heaven.

55:53.976 --> 55:55.059
I swear.

55:58.689 --> 56:00.398
Hah!

56:07.489 --> 56:08.739
You won't say?

56:08.740 --> 56:11.909
You know I won't hesitate
to cut you.

56:11.910 --> 56:13.995
I am gonna check the ledgers.

56:13.996 --> 56:16.999
So why don't you just spit it out,
fucking bitch?

56:26.383 --> 56:30.011
No, Heeju!
No, don't do it.

56:42.316 --> 56:45.234
Go.
Hurry, hurry, go.

56:45.235 --> 56:47.153
Look at me and get a hold of yourself!

56:47.154 --> 56:49.196
Just grab what you need and go.

56:49.197 --> 56:50.449
I'll take care of everything.
:cue

57:13.180 --> 57:15.432
Take this.
It's the money I've earned over the years.

57:16.475 --> 57:17.809
I've been saving it for you.

57:19.978 --> 57:22.521
So take it and don't ever come back.

57:22.522 --> 57:26.442
No matter what happens to me,
don't try to look for me.

57:26.443 --> 57:27.444
Don't try to find out.

57:28.445 --> 57:29.821
You go somewhere far away.

57:30.864 --> 57:32.491
I want you to live a good life.

57:33.492 --> 57:34.493
No.

57:35.786 --> 57:37.828
You have to go.

57:37.829 --> 57:40.539
I'm really sorry.
Heeju.

57:40.540 --> 57:42.667
I'm sorry.

57:42.668 --> 57:45.294
I need you to listen.
Just listen to me this once.

57:45.295 --> 57:47.421
Go! You going will save my life.

57:47.422 --> 57:49.799
Go. Go!

57:49.800 --> 57:51.801
Auntie! Auntie!

57:51.802 --> 57:52.885
-  Go!
-  Auntie!

57:54.971 --> 57:58.392
I told you to go! Go!
Hurry up and get outta here!

58:00.268 --> 58:02.812
I said go away! Go!

58:39.141 --> 58:40.142
Hello.

58:40.684 --> 58:43.729
I-I'm in Bukju.

58:45.439 --> 58:47.399
The Happy Pawnshop in Bukju.

58:48.734 --> 58:52.571
I think I killed a person.

59:35.989 --> 59:37.281
Auntie.

59:39.618 --> 59:40.826
Mom.
